<section class="section section--hero">
  <div class="content stack">
    <span class="eyebrow">Grant guidelines</span>
    <h1 class="display">Who we fund, and <em>how</em>.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Grants go to 501(c)(3) organizations, not to individuals. We focus on Christian sacred spaces, with room for related work.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--page">
  <div class="wrap grid grid--2">
    <div class="card card--lg card--accent card--interactive">
      <h3 class="card__title card__title--list">What a grant can pay for</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><i class="ph ph-check icon icon--sm icon--brass" aria-hidden="true"></i>Bell repair, rehanging, and new rings</li>
        <li><i class="ph ph-check icon icon--sm icon--brass" aria-hidden="true"></i>Tower frames, headstocks and fittings</li>
        <li><i class="ph ph-check icon icon--sm icon--brass" aria-hidden="true"></i>Electronic carillons for churches without bells</li>
        <li><i class="ph ph-check icon icon--sm icon--brass" aria-hidden="true"></i>Pipe organ restoration, purchase and tuning</li>
        <li><i class="ph ph-check icon icon--sm icon--brass" aria-hidden="true"></i>Rose windows, stained glass and leadwork</li>
        <li><i class="ph ph-check icon icon--sm icon--brass" aria-hidden="true"></i>Training artisans and apprentices in the sacred arts</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card card--lg card--sunk card--interactive">
      <h3 class="card__title card__title--list">What it cannot</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><i class="ph ph-x icon icon--sm icon--rose" aria-hidden="true"></i>Requests from individuals</li>
        <li><i class="ph ph-x icon icon--sm icon--rose" aria-hidden="true"></i>Salaries, operating costs and debt</li>
        <li><i class="ph ph-x icon icon--sm icon--rose" aria-hidden="true"></i>General building work unrelated to bells, organs or glass</li>
        <li><i class="ph ph-x icon icon--sm icon--rose" aria-hidden="true"></i>Political or campaign activity</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--sunk">
  <div class="content stack">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">Electronic carillons</span>
      <h2>For churches without bells</h2>
    </header>
    <p class="m0">A church without a tower can still ring. An electronic carillon brings the sound of cast bronze bells through speakers set in a steeple or on an exterior wall, with nothing to cast, nothing to build, and no structure to reinforce. It rings the Call to Worship and the Angelus, peals for weddings, tolls for funerals, and keeps Westminster chimes with the hour. Its library holds thousands of hymns, Ave Maria and Gregorian chant among them. A grant can cover one.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--band">
  <div class="wrap grid grid--steps">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it goes</span>
      <h2>Three steps, and a conversation</h2>
      <p class="lede">The first form is short on purpose. Documents come later, and only if we ask.</p>
    </header>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <span class="steps__num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Send a short inquiry</h3>
          <p>The form on this site takes a few minutes. No documents yet.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="steps__num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <div>
          <h3>We read and reply</h3>
          <p>We will read all submissions and reply.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="steps__num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Further information</h3>
          <p>If a request passes the first review, we will ask for additional information such as budget plans, photographs, drawings, and a cost estimate.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
